# One physically measured mass transfer, agent -> orchestrator — FR-ISRU-2 /
# FR-DASH-7 (deviation D-06).
#
# Published by selene_agent on /orchestrator/material_event whenever an
# ExcavateSkill or HaulSkill finishes a transfer whose mass was READ FROM A
# SENSOR. Nothing here is estimated, inferred, or derived from a task count:
# every mass_kg below is the difference of two FillLevelReading.mass_kg values,
# which the HAL derives from the RCDL capacity_kg of that sensor
# (selene_hal/config/*.yaml). A skill that cannot read its fill sensor
# publishes NOTHING rather than a zero.
#
# NO POSITION FIELD, DELIBERATELY, AND STILL SO AFTER THE FRAME FIX. A site is
# identified by the orchestrator's own site_id, resolved from task_id via
# TaskQueue (TaskEntry.site_id).
#
# The original reason was that a position here would have been a dead-reckoned
# /odom pose — DiffDrive integrates from each robot's spawn pose, so two robots
# at the same physical place reported different coordinates (register D-08).
# That specific hazard is gone: since 2026-07-31 position is world-referenced
# (selene_sim/selene_sim/world_odometry_node.py) and two robots at one place
# agree.
#
# The field stays absent because the WEAKER reason was always the load-bearing
# one: the pose is still DEAD-RECKONED, so two robots at one place agree only up
# to their accumulated wheel slip, and a site keyed on position would split into
# several the moment that slip exceeded whatever tolerance the key used. An id
# has no tolerance to get wrong.
#
# DELIVERY. Publisher and subscriber both use RELIABLE + TRANSIENT_LOCAL,
# KEEP_LAST(100). This is the ledger: a dropped sample is mass that vanishes
# from mission progress with nothing logged. Transient-local means an
# orchestrator that starts (or restarts) after an agent still receives that
# agent's history, and event_id below makes the replay idempotent. Depth 100 is
# ~6x the events a 100 kg mission generates (5 excavate + 5 haul = 15).
# NOT VERIFIED: Fast DDS transient-local replay behaviour could not be exercised
# on the machine this was designed on. The design degrades to LOST HISTORY, never
# to double-counted mass, if that assumption is wrong.

# Globally unique, generated by the publishing agent as
#     "<robot_id>:<node_start_epoch_ns>:<counter:06d>"
# The orchestrator keeps the last 4096 ids and ignores a repeat. The epoch term
# is what makes an agent restart produce fresh ids instead of colliding with its
# own pre-restart history; the counter — rather than task_id — is what stops a
# RETRIED task (same task_id, re-queued after an interruption) from being
# discarded as a duplicate of its own failed attempt.
string event_id

# Publishing robot, and the task it was executing. task_id is how the
# orchestrator resolves the site: TaskQueue.get_task(task_id).site_id. An event
# whose task is unknown, or whose task carries no site_id, is DROPPED with a
# WARNING FleetAlert — never credited to a site invented on the spot.
string robot_id
string task_id

# "extracted" | "loaded" | "unloaded". Lower-case strings rather than uint8
# constants, matching RobotState.fsm_state, FleetAlert.severity,
# TaskAnnouncement.task_type and SetRobotCommand.command. It also keeps the
# ROS-free stub in selene_orchestrator/test/conftest.py a plain field bag with
# no class constants to mirror.
#   extracted -> MaterialInventory.record_extraction(site_id, robot_id, mass_kg)
#   loaded    -> MaterialInventory.record_load(robot_id, site_id, mass_kg)
#   unloaded  -> MaterialInventory.record_unload(robot_id, mass_kg)
string event_type

# Mass moved by THIS event, kg, always >= 0. A difference of two readings:
#   extracted: hopper mass at hopper-full (or drill timeout) minus the hopper
#              mass recorded at the start of the DRILLING phase.
#   loaded:    bin mass once loading settled minus bin mass on arrival.
#   unloaded:  bin mass before the dump minus bin mass after it.
float32 mass_kg

# The sensor's ABSOLUTE reading immediately after the event, kg. Carried so the
# orchestrator can cross-check the delta against the instrument that produced
# it: a hauler reporting 19 kg unloaded while its load cell still reads 7 kg is
# a fault this field makes visible, and FR-ISRU-2's acceptance ("no material is
# lost or duplicated") is exactly that kind of statement. Expected near 0 after
# "unloaded", and after "extracted" because the excavator dumps its hopper
# before the skill completes.
float32 residual_mass_kg

# Agent wall clock at the moment the transfer completed. NOT simulation time:
# use_sim_time is unset repo-wide (0 code occurrences).
builtin_interfaces/Time stamp
